't make a mistake.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nTens: 2 + 4 = 6\n\nHundreds: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1 in thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\nThousands: 7 + 0 = 7\n\nTen-thousands: 2 + 2 = 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 6 = 11 \u2192 1 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nTen-millions: 5 + 6 = 11 \u2192 1 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\nSo the sum is 111,097,969, which is 11 digits. Let me verify that again.\n\nWait, 750,287,621 + 360,102,348. Let's add each digit:\n\nUnits: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nTens: 2 + 4 = 6\n\nHundreds: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1 in thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\nThousands: 7 + 0 = 7\n\nTen-thousands: 2 + 2 = 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 6 = 11 \u2192 1 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nTen-millions: 5 + 6 = 11 \u2192 1 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\nSo the sum is 111,097,969. Let me check the addition again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n2 + 4 = 6\n\n8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1 in thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\n7 + 0 = 7\n\n2 + 2 = 4\n\n5 + 6 = 11 \u2192 1 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n0 + 0 = 0\n\n1 + 1 = 2\n\nSo the sum is 111,097,969. Let me check the addition again step by step.\n\nFirst, add the units: 1 + 8 = 9. Correct.\n\nTens: 2 + 4 = 6. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 3 = 11. So 1 in thousands, 1 in ten-thousands. So 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 2,000,000. Then 1,00