      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 685,497,553 and 418,270,610. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n685,497,553\n+ 418,270,610\n\nFirst, I should line them up by their place values. Let's align them like this:\n\n  685,497,553\n+ 418,270,610\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I'll add each corresponding digit. Let's go step by step.\n\nUnits place: 3 + 0 = 3. So that's 3 in the units place.\n\nTens place: 5 + 1 = 6. So that's 6 in the tens place.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 0 = 7. So that's 7 in the hundreds place.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 8 = 13. So that's 3 in the thousands place and 1 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6. So that's 6 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 8 + 1 = 9. So that's 9 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nMillions place: 5 + 8 = 13. So that's 3 in the millions place and 1 in the ten-millions place.\n\nTen-millions place: 6 + 4 = 10. So that's 0 in the ten-millions place and 1 in the hundred-millions place.\n\nHundred-millions place: 8 + 1 = 9. So that's 9 in the hundred-millions place.\n\nSo putting all those together, the sum should be:\n\n900,000,000 (hundred-millions place)\n+ 100,000,000 (ten-millions place)\n+ 1,000,000 (millions place)\n+ 3,000,000 (ten-thousands place)\n+ 6,000 (thousands place)\n+ 130 (hundreds place)\n+ 6 (tens place)\n+ 3 (units place)\n\nAdding these up:\n\n900,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,000,000,000\n1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,001,000,000\n1,001,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 1,004,000,000\n1,004,000,000 + 6,000 = 1,004,006,000\n1,004,006,000 + 130 = 1,004,006,130\n1,004,006,130 + 6 = 1,004,006,136\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's add them step by step:\n\n1. 900,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,000,000,000\n2. 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,001,000,000\n3. 1,001,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 1,004,000,000\n4. 1,004,000,000 + 6,000 = 1,004,006,000\n5. 1,004,006,000 + 130 = 1,004,006,130\n6. 1,004,006,130 + 6 = 1,004,006,136\n\nYes, that seems right. So the sum is 1,004,006,136. Let me verify by adding the numbers directly:\n\n685,497,553 + 418,270,610\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n5 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5 in ten-thousands, 1 in hundred-thousands\n\n5 + 2 = 7\n\n4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n6 + 4 = 10 \u2192 0 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3 in hundred-thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\n4 + 2 = 6\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n900,000,000 (hundred-millions)\n+ 100,000,000 (ten-millions)\n+ 1,000,000 (millions)\n+ 3,000,000 (ten-thousands)\n+ 6,000 (thousands)\n+ 130 (hundreds)\n+ 6 (tens)\n+ 3 (units)\n\nAdding these:\n\n900,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,000,000,000\n\n1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,001,000,000\n\n1,001,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 1,004,000,000\n\n1,004,000,000 + 6,000 = 1,004,006,000\n\n1,004,006,000 + 130 = 1,004,006,130\n\n1,004,006,130 + 6 = 1,004,006,136\n\nYep, that's correct. So the sum is 1,004,006,136. Let me just check if there's any mistake in the addition. For example, when adding 685,497,553 and 418,270,610, maybe I can add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n5 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5 in ten-thousands, 1 in hundred-thousands\n\n5 + 2 = 7\n\n4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n6 + 4 = 10 \u2192 0 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3 in hundred-thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\n4 + 2 = 6\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\nSo that's 1,004,006,136. Seems right. Alternatively, maybe I can use the standard addition method. Let's try that:\n\nAligning the numbers:\n\n  685,497,553\n+ 418,270,610\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n5 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5 in ten-thousands, 1 in hundred-thousands\n\n5 + 2 = 7\n\n4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n6 + 4 = 10 \u2192 0 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n8 + 1 = 9\n\n5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3 in hundred-thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\n4 + 2 = 6\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\nSo adding them step by step:\n\n1. 3 + 0 = 3\n\n2. 5 + 1 = 6\n\n3. 7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5 in ten-thousands, 1 in hundred-thousands\n\n4. 5 + 2 = 7\n\n5. 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n6. 8 + 1 = 9\n\n7. 5 + 0 = 5\n\n8. 6 + 4 = 10 \u2192 0 in ten-millions, 1 in hundred-millions\n\n9. 8 + 1 = 9\n\n10. 5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3 in hundred-thousands, 1 in ten-thousands\n\n11. 4 + 2 = 6\n\n12. 6 + 0 = 6\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\n900,000,000 (hundred-millions)\n+ 100,000,000 (ten-millions)\n+ 1,000,000 (millions)\n+ 3,000,000 (ten-thousands)\n+ 6,000 (thousands)\n+ 130 (hundreds)\n+ 6 (tens)\n+ 3 (units)\n\nAdding these:\n\n900,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,000,000,000\n\n1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,001,000,000\n\n1,001,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 1,004,000,000\n\n1,004,000,000 + 6,000 = 1,004,006,000\n\n1,004,006,000 + 130 = 1,004,006,130\n\n1,004,006,130 + 6 = 1,004,006,136\n\nYes, same result. So the sum is 1,004,006,136. Therefore, the answer is 1,004,006,136.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nTo find the sum of \\(685,497,553\\) and \\(418,270,610\\), we align the numbers by their place values and add digit by digit:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  685,497,553 \\\\\n+ 418,270,610 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\\[\n3 + 0 = 3\n\\]\n\nNext digits (tens place):\n\\[\n5 + 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nNext digits (hundreds place):\n\\[\n7 + 8 = 15 \\quad \\text{(write 5, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (thousands place):\n\\[\n5 + 2 = 7 \\quad \\text{(add carry 1: 8)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (ten-thousands place):\n\\[\n4 + 8 = 12 \\quad \\text{(write 2, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (hundred-thousands place):\n\\[\n8 + 1 = 9 \\quad \\text{(add carry 1: 10, write 0, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (millions place):\n\\[\n5 + 8 = 13 \\quad \\text{(write 3, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (ten-millions place):\n\\[\n6 + 1 = 7 \\quad \\text{(add carry 1: 8)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (hundred-millions place):\n\\[\n8 + 1 = 9 \\quad \\text{(add carry 1: 10, write 0, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (ten-millions place):\n\\[\n4 + 0 = 4 \\quad \\text{(add carry 1: 5)}\n\\]\n\nNext digits (hundred-millions place):\n\\[\n6 + 0 = 6\n\\]\n\nNext digits (ten-millions place):\n\\[\n1 + 4 = 5\n\\]\n\nNext digits (hundred-millions place):\n\\[\n3 + 6 = 9\n\\]\n\nSumming all the digits:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  900,000,000 \\\\\n+ 100,000,000 \\\\\n+ 1,000,000 \\\\\n+ 3,000,000 \\\\\n+ 6,000 \\\\\n+ 130 \\\\\n+ 6 \\\\\n\\hline\n  1,004,006,136 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThe final sum is \\(\\boxed{1004006136}\\).\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
