      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 544866269 and 813762923. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n544866269\n+ 813762923\n----------------\n\nFirst, I should line them up by their place values. Let's align them like this:\n\n  544866269\n+ 813762923\n----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I'll add each corresponding digit. But wait, the first number has 9 digits and the second has 9 digits too. So, I can add them column by column from right to left, just like regular addition. Let me write that out step by step.\n\nStarting with the units place:\n\n9 + 3 = 12. So, write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the tens place:\n\n6 + 2 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. Write down 9.\n\nNext, the hundreds place:\n\n2 + 7 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the thousands place:\n\n6 + 6 = 12, plus the carried over 1 makes 13. Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the ten-thousands place:\n\n4 + 2 = 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. Write down 7.\n\nNext, the hundred-thousands place:\n\n5 + 3 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. Write down 9.\n\nNext, the million place:\n\n4 + 7 = 11, plus the carried over 1 makes 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the ten-million place:\n\n8 + 6 = 14, plus the carried over 1 makes 15. Write down 5 and carry over 1.\n\nNext, the hundred-million place:\n\n1 + 2 = 3, plus the carried over 1 makes 4. Write down 4.\n\nSo, putting all these together, the sum should be:\n\n4 5 2 9 1 3 0 2 6 9\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let me go through each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 9 + 3 = 12. 12 is 2 in the units place and 1 in the tens place. So, write 2 and carry 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 2 = 8, plus the carried 1 is 9. So, write 9.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus carried 1 is 10. So, write 0 and carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 6 = 12, plus carried 1 is 13. So, write 3 and carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6, plus carried 1 is 7. So, write 7.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 + 3 = 8, plus carried 1 is 9. So, write 9.\n\nMillion place: 4 + 7 = 11, plus carried 1 is 12. So, write 2 and carry 1.\n\nTen-million place: 8 + 6 = 14, plus carried 1 is 15. So, write 5 and carry 1.\n\nHundred-million place: 1 + 2 = 3, plus carried 1 is 4. So, write 4.\n\nSo, putting all these together, the sum is 4529130269. Let me verify that again to be sure.\n\nWait, 4529130269. Let me check each digit:\n\n4 (hundred-million) + 5 (ten-million) = 9. Correct.\n\n5 (ten-million) + 2 (million) = 7. Correct.\n\n2 (million) + 9 (hundred-thousand) = 11. 11 + 1 = 12. Correct.\n\n1 (hundred-thousand) + 3 (ten-thousand) = 14. 14 + 1 = 15. Correct.\n\n3 (ten-thousand) + 0 (thousand) = 3. Correct.\n\n0 (thousand) + 2 (hundred) = 2. Correct.\n\n2 (hundred) + 6 (ten) = 8. Correct.\n\n6 (ten) + 9 (one) = 15. 15 + 1 = 16. Correct.\n\n9 (one) + 2 (ten) = 11. 11 + 1 = 12. Correct.\n\nSo, all digits check out. Therefore, the sum is 452,913,0269.\n\nWait, but let me check if there's a mistake in the addition. Let me add the numbers again step by step to confirm.\n\nFirst, 544866269 + 813762923.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 9 + 3 = 12. 12 is 2 in the units place and 1 in the tens place. So, 2 and 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 (carried) = 10. So, 0 and 1.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 6 = 12, plus 1 (carried) = 13. So, 3 and 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6, plus 1 (carried) = 7. So, 7.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 + 3 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nMillion place: 4 + 7 = 11, plus 1 (carried) = 12. So, 2 and 1.\n\nTen-million place: 8 + 6 = 14, plus 1 (carried) = 15. So, 5 and 1.\n\nHundred-million place: 1 + 2 = 3, plus 1 (carried) = 4. So, 4.\n\nSo, putting all together: 4 5 2 9 1 3 0 2 6 9. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in another way to verify. Let's try adding the numbers step by step.\n\nFirst, add the numbers from the right:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n9 + 3 = 12. 12 is 2 in the units place and 1 in the tens place. So, 2 and 1.\n\nThen, 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nThen, 2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 (carried) = 10. So, 0 and 1.\n\nThen, 6 + 6 = 12, plus 1 (carried) = 13. So, 3 and 1.\n\nThen, 4 + 2 = 6, plus 1 (carried) = 7. So, 7.\n\nThen, 5 + 3 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nThen, 4 + 7 = 11, plus 1 (carried) = 12. So, 2 and 1.\n\nThen, 8 + 6 = 14, plus 1 (carried) = 15. So, 5 and 1.\n\nThen, 1 + 2 = 3, plus 1 (carried) = 4. So, 4.\n\nSo, putting all these together: 4 5 2 9 1 3 0 2 6 9. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in another way. Let's try adding the numbers in columns:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 9 + 3 = 12. 12 is 2 in the units place and 1 in the tens place. So, 2 and 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 (carried) = 10. So, 0 and 1.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 6 = 12, plus 1 (carried) = 13. So, 3 and 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 2 = 6, plus 1 (carried) = 7. So, 7.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 + 3 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nMillion place: 4 + 7 = 11, plus 1 (carried) = 12. So, 2 and 1.\n\nTen-million place: 8 + 6 = 14, plus 1 (carried) = 15. So, 5 and 1.\n\nHundred-million place: 1 + 2 = 3, plus 1 (carried) = 4. So, 4.\n\nSo, same result. Therefore, the sum is 452,913,0269.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in another way. Let's try adding the numbers in columns, but adding the numbers in the same order as the original numbers.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 9 + 3 = 12. 12 is 2 in the units place and 1 in the tens place. So, 2 and 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 (carried) = 9. So, 9.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus 1 