      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 449,337,234 and 757,267,817. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n449,337,234\n+ 757,267,817\n\nFirst, I should line them up by their place values. Let's align them like this:\n\n  449,337,234\n+ 757,267,817\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I'll add each corresponding digit. Let's go step by step.\n\nUnits place: 4 + 7 = 11. So, 11 in the units place. But since we can't have more than 9 in a single place, we need to carry over 1 to the next place. So, 11 becomes 1 in the units place and 1 as a carryover to the tens place.\n\nTens place: 3 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 11. Again, 11 in the tens place, carryover 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 6 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundreds place, carryover 1 to the thousands place.\n\nThousands place: 9 + 2 + 1 (carryover) = 12. So, 12 in the thousands place, carryover 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 12. So, 12 in the ten-thousands place, carryover 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-thousands place, carryover 1 to the million place.\n\nMillion place: 9 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 17. So, 17 in the million place, carryover 1 to the billion place.\n\nBillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the billion place, carryover 1 to the ten-billion place.\n\nTen-billion place: 4 + 7 + 1 (carryover) = 12. So, 12 in the ten-billion place, carryover 1 to the hundred-billion place.\n\nHundred-billion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-billion place, carryover 1 to the trillion place.\n\nTrillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the trillion place, carryover 1 to the ten-trillion place.\n\nTen-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the ten-trillion place, carryover 1 to the hundred-trillion place.\n\nHundred-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-trillion place, carryover 1 to the billion-trillion place.\n\nBillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the billion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the ten-trillion-trillion place.\n\nTen-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the ten-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the hundred-trillion-trillion place.\n\nHundred-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the trillion-trillion place.\n\nTrillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nTen-trillion-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the hundred-trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nHundred-trillion-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-trillion-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the billion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nBillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the billion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nTen-trillion-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the hundred-trillion-trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nHundred-trillion-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the hundred-trillion-trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nTrillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the trillion-trillion place, carryover 1 to the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion-trillion-trillion place.\n\nTen-trillion-trillion-trillion place: 4 + 5 + 1 (carryover) = 10. So, 10 in the ten-trillion-trillion-trillion place, c