      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 342,376,364 and 355,952,862. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n342,376,364\n+ 355,952,862\n\nFirst, I should line them up by their place values. Let's align them like this:\n\n  342,376,364\n+ 355,952,862\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I can add each corresponding digit. Let's go step by step.\n\nUnits place: 4 + 2 = 6. So that's 6 in the units place.\n\nTens place: 6 + 6 = 12. So 2 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 5 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. So 9 in the hundreds place.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 5 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So 8 in the thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 9 = 12. So 2 in the ten-thousands place and carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 5 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So 0 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 1 to the million place.\n\nMillion place: 2 + 5 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So 8 in the million place.\n\nTen-millions place: 3 + 5 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. So 9 in the ten-millions place.\n\nHundred-millions place: 3 + 3 = 6, plus the carried over 1 makes 7. So 7 in the hundred-millions place.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum should be 700,339,226. Let me check that again to make sure I didn't make any mistakes.\n\nStarting from the units place: 4 + 2 = 6. Correct.\n\nTens place: 6 + 6 = 12, carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 5 = 8, plus 1 (carry) = 9. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 5 = 7, plus 1 (carry) = 8. Correct.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 9 = 12, carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 5 = 9, plus 1 (carry) = 10, so 0, carry 1. Correct.\n\nMillion place: 2 + 5 = 7, plus 1 (carry) = 8. Correct.\n\nTen-millions place: 3 + 5 = 8, plus 1 (carry) = 9. Correct.\n\nHundred-millions place: 3 + 3 = 6, plus 1 (carry) = 7. Correct.\n\nSo the sum is indeed 700,339,226. Let me verify by adding the numbers directly:\n\n342,376,364\n+ 355,952,862\n----------------\nAdding from right to left:\n\nUnits: 4 + 2 = 6\nTens: 6 + 6 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\nHundreds: 3 + 5 = 8, +1 (carry) = 9\nThousands: 2 + 5 = 7, +1 (carry) = 8\nTen-thousands: 3 + 9 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 5 = 9, +1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\nMillion: 2 + 5 = 7, +1 (carry) = 8\nTen-millions: 3 + 5 = 8, +1 (carry) = 9\nHundred-millions: 3 + 3 = 6, +1 (carry) = 7\n\nSo putting it all together: 700,339,226. Yep, that seems right. I don't see any errors in the calculation. Let me just check the addition again step by step to be thorough.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 2 = 6\n\n6 + 6 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n3 + 5 = 8, +1 (carry) = 9\n\n2 + 5 = 7, +1 (carry) = 8\n\n3 + 9 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n4 + 5 = 9, +1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n2 + 5 = 7, +1 (carry) = 8\n\n3 + 3 = 6, +1 (carry) = 7\n\nSo the sum is 700,339,226. That's correct. I think that's all. No mistakes detected in the process. The key was breaking down the addition into manageable parts and checking each step carefully. I don't see any errors in the calculations. So the answer should be 700,339,226.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nTo find the sum of \\(342,376,364\\) and \\(355,952,862\\), we align the numbers by their place values and add digit by digit, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  342,376,364 \\\\\n+ 355,952,862 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n- \\(4 + 2 = 6\\)\n- \\(6 + 6 = 12\\) (write 2, carry 1)\n- \\(3 + 5 = 8\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(2 + 5 = 7\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(3 + 9 = 12\\) (write 2, carry 1)\n- \\(4 + 5 = 9\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(2 + 5 = 7\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(3 + 3 = 6\\) (carry 1)\n\nNext, adding the carries:\n- \\(0 + 1 = 1\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n- \\(1 + 1 = 2\\) (carry 1)\n\nSumming all digits:\n- Units: \\(6\\)\n- Tens: \\(2\\)\n- Hundreds: \\(9\\)\n- Thousands: \\(8\\)\n- Ten-thousands: \\(7\\)\n- Hundred-thousands: \\(8\\)\n- Million: \\(9\\)\n- Ten-millions: \\(7\\)\n- Hundred-millions: \\(7\\)\n\nThus, the total sum is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{700339226}\n\\]\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
