arry 1.\n\n2 + 2 = 4. Add 1 (carry) = 5.\n\n7 + 0 = 7. Add 1 (carry) = 8.\n\n0 + 2 = 2. Add 1 (carry) = 3.\n\n7 + 2 = 9. Add 1 (carry) = 10. So 0, carry 1.\n\n8 + 8 = 16. Add 1 (carry) = 17. So 7, carry 1.\n\n4 + 7 = 11. Add 1 (carry) = 12. So 2, carry 1.\n\n2 + 8 = 10. Add 1 (carry) = 11. So 1, carry 1.\n\n8 + 3 = 11. Add 1 (carry) = 12. So 6.\n\nSo the sum is 617,949,156. That seems correct. I think that's the right answer.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nTo find the sum of \\(248,708,728\\) and \\(378,220,428\\), we align the numbers by their place values and add digit by digit:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  248,708,728 \\\\\n+ 378,220,428 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n\\[\n8 + 8 = 16 \\quad \\text{(write 6, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 + 2 = 4 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 5)}\n\\]\n\\[\n7 + 0 = 7 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 8)}\n\\]\n\\[\n0 + 2 = 2 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 3)}\n\\]\n\\[\n7 + 2 = 9 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 10. Write 0, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n8 + 8 = 16 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 17. Write 7, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n4 + 7 = 11 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 12. Write 2, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n2 + 8 = 10 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 11. Write 1, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\\[\n8 + 3 = 11 \\quad \\text{(add 1, write 12. Write 6, carry 1)}\n\\]\n\nSumming the carries: \\(1 + 1 + 1 = 3\\).\n\nThus, the final sum is \\(617,949,156\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{617949156}\n\\]\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
