      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 589,473,790 and 219,574,375. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n589,473,790\n+ 219,574,375\n\nFirst, I should line them up by their place values. Let's align them like this:\n\n  589,473,790\n+ 219,574,375\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I can add each corresponding digit. Let's go step by step.\n\nUnits place: 0 + 5 = 5. So that's 5 in the units place.\n\nTens place: 9 + 7 = 16. But since we're adding two numbers, we need to carry over 1 to the tens place. So that's 6 in the tens place and 1 in the hundreds place.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 4 = 11. Again, carry over 1 to the hundreds place. So 1 in the hundreds place and 1 in the thousands place.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 9 = 12. Carry over 1 to the ten-thousands place. So 2 in the ten-thousands place and 1 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 + 5 = 12. Carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place. So 1 in the hundred-thousands place and 2 in the millions place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 1 = 5. No carryover here.\n\nMillions place: 8 + 2 = 10. Carry over 1 to the ten-millions place. So 1 in the ten-millions place and 0 in the hundred-millions place.\n\nTen-millions place: 9 + 1 = 10. Carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place. So 1 in the hundred-millions place and 0 in the billion place.\n\nHundred-millions place: 5 + 0 = 5. No carryover here.\n\nBillion place: 0 + 0 = 0. No carryover here.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum should be:\n\n1,000,000,000 (from the hundred-millions place) + 100,000,000 (from the ten-millions place) + 10,000,000 (from the hundred-thousands place) + 2,000,000 (from the ten-thousands place) + 1,000,000 (from the thousands place) + 600,000 (from the hundreds place) + 100,000 (from the tens place) + 5 (from the units place) = 1,100,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,200,000,000 + 10,000,000 = 1,210,000,000 + 2,000,000 = 1,212,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,213,000,000 + 600,000 = 1,213,600,000 + 100,000 = 1,213,700,000 + 5 = 1,213,700,005.\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's add step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 0 + 5 = 5\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16. 16 + 1 (carryover) = 17. 17 + 1 (carryover) = 18. So 8 in tens place, 1 in hundreds place.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 4 = 11. 11 + 1 (carryover) = 12. 12 + 1 (carryover) = 13. So 3 in hundreds place, 1 in thousands place.\n\nThousands: 3 + 9 = 12. 12 + 1 (carryover) = 13. 13 + 1 (carryover) = 14. So 4 in thousands place, 1 in ten-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 5 = 12. 12 + 1 (carryover) = 13. 13 + 1 (carryover) = 14. So 4 in ten-thousands place, 1 in hundred-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 1 = 5. 5 + 1 (carryover) = 6. So 6 in hundred-thousands place.\n\nMillions: 8 + 2 = 10. 10 + 1 (carryover) = 11. So 1 in ten-millions place, 1 in hundred-millions place.\n\nTen-millions: 9 + 1 = 10. 10 + 1 (carryover) = 11. So 1 in hundred-millions place, 1 in billion place.\n\nBillion: 0 + 0 = 0. 0 + 1 (carryover) = 1. So 1 in billion place.\n\nSo the sum is 1,213,700,005. Let me verify that again.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,213,700,005\n\n1,